#AUTO 61
#NEEDED 0
# Whole-DRAM striped march (issue 110n) — DE-SELECTED by default.
#
# The routine dram-walk probe (@60) tests a 1 MB window. This is the thorough
# version: a striped march (one word per 4 KB page) across the whole 2 GB
# above the kernel (0x40000000..0xC0000000), for when you actually suspect
# bad RAM. Four marching patterns plus an address-in-address pass, reporting
# the first failing word.
#
# DE-SELECTED by default: it is slow (caches off) and clobbers that whole 2 GB
# range, so it is a deliberate on-demand check, not a routine one. The 1 MB
# walk is enough for the boot health report. DRAM only (never a peripheral);
# done in C behind a CALL because the interpreter's W is peripheral-only.

CALL memtest_full
